class Solution {
    public int[] productExceptSelf(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int[] answer = new int[n];

        // Step 1: Build prefix products
        answer[0] = 1; // no elements before index 0
        for(int i=1; i<n; i++){
            answer[i] = nums[i - 1] * answer[i - 1];  // answer[i] holds product of all elements before index i
        }

        // Step 2: Multiply by suffix products
        int suffix=1;  // suffix product starts as 1 (no elements after last index)
        for(int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--){
            answer[i] = answer[i] * suffix; //ans[i]=prefix*suffix
            suffix *= nums[i]; // update suffix product by multiplying with current element
        }
        return answer;                    
    }
}



Time Complexity: O(n) (two passes).
Space Complexity: O(1) extra (just one variable for suffix).
